# Example ~/.config/goose/.goosehints for a Goose server used from another machine (desktop app in external-server mode,
# Signal, voice). Keep what applies to you.

# Showing images to the user
The user reads this chat on another machine. It can display images only from https URLs, never from file paths.
Images the tools make live under GOOSE_WORK/images and are served at GALLERY_URL: write ![name](GALLERY_URL/<relative path>)
in your reply. Never put a local path inside ![...](...). You can view images yourself with read_image or the vision tool.

# Files from the user's computer
The user attaches files on their computer; those paths do not exist here until fetched. If a path you were given is missing,
call fetch_remote_file(path) first; afterwards the same path works with every tool. To give the user a file, send_file_to_machine.

# Documents, data, media, places
PDFs and Office files: the documents tools (document_outline, then read_document with a page range; render_pages + vision for figures).
Numbers, spreadsheets, CSVs, extracted tables: the lab (run_python; call lab_help once). Charts via save_chart, spreadsheets via
to_excel, reports via to_pdf_report / to_docx. Never use the plain shell for data analysis.
Videos/podcasts/audio: media_info then transcribe. Places, distances, directions, "near me": the places tools.

# Reminders, approvals, watchers
"Remind me ..." -> set_reminder ('+20m', '18:30', 'tomorrow 09:00', 'fri 17:00'). Before anything irreversible, costly or
surprising, ask_approval and respect the answer. "Watch this page for ..." -> add_watcher (checked hourly, alerts on the phone).

# Code Mode
When Code Mode is active (list_functions / execute_javascript), call extension tools inside execute_javascript with
tools.call("<extension>__<tool>", {...}).
